---
/**
 * Terms of service. Written plainly; covers what Paddle's review requires: the
 * seller's legal name, the Merchant of Record disclosure, acceptable use, rights
 * in what you upload and get back (media editing and AI tools), a takedown
 * route, no guarantee of service, suspension, and contact.
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
import { CONTACT, REFUND_DAYS, SELLER, SELLER_KIND, UPDATED } from '../data/legal'
---

<Page title="Terms · Inlay" description="The terms for using Inlay, its free app and its paid HD mode.">
  <article class="prose" aria-labelledby="terms-title">
    <h1 id="terms-title">Terms</h1>
    <p class="lede">The rules for using Inlay, in plain words.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Inlay (inlaytrace.com) is operated by {SELLER}, {SELLER_KIND} ("we", "us"). You can reach us at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. By using the site, the app or HD mode, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree,
      please don't use them.
    </p>

    <h2>What Inlay is</h2>
    <p>
      Inlay turns images into vector graphics. The app is free: it runs in your browser and your images stay on your device. HD mode is an
      optional, paid service that processes an image on our servers, paid for with credits (see <a href="/pricing/">pricing</a>). The
      tracer's source code is open source under the MIT licence; that licence, not these terms, covers the code itself.
    </p>

    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>
      Our order process is conducted by our online reseller Paddle.com. Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record for all our orders. Paddle
      provides all customer service inquiries and handles returns. Paddle's <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/checkout-buyer-terms"
        >buyer terms</a> apply to your purchase.
    </p>
    <p>
      Credits are sold in packs, never expire, have no cash value and can't be transferred to another account. An HD run uses the credits
      the app shows before you start it; a run that fails gives them back. You can get a full refund within {REFUND_DAYS} days under our{' '}
      <a href="/refunds/">refund policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      You need an account to buy and use credits, and not for anything else. Keep access to your email address safe: anyone who can open
      the sign-in links we send can use your credits. You can delete your account at any time from the account page; unused credits are
      lost when you do.
    </p>

    <h2>Your images and results</h2>
    <p>
      You keep all rights in the images you open and the results you make. When you use HD mode, you give us permission to process that
      image only to produce your result; we delete it as soon as the result is back, and we don't use it for anything else, including
      training.
    </p>
    <p>
      You're responsible for having the right to use the images you process and for how you use the results. Results are produced
      automatically and may be inaccurate or incomplete, so check them before you rely on them, especially for anything regulated, like
      medical, legal or engineering work.
    </p>

    <h2>What you may not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Break the law, or process images you don't have the right to use, including anything that infringes someone's copyright or trademark.</li>
      <li>Process sexual images of real people without their consent, any sexual content involving minors, or images meant to harass, threaten, deceive or expose someone (including their private information).</li>
      <li>Use Inlay for fraud, spam or malware.</li>
      <li>Attack, probe, overload or scrape the service, or try to get around its limits, payments or safeguards.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reporting infringing material</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe Inlay is being used to infringe your rights, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> with what you believe is
      infringed and where. We'll look into it promptly and act where it's justified. We'll close the accounts of people who repeatedly
      infringe others' rights.
    </p>

    <h2>Suspension and ending</h2>
    <p>
      We may suspend or close an account that seriously or repeatedly breaks these terms, puts the service or other people at risk, or is used
      for fraud, including chargebacks made in bad faith. Where we close an account without good cause, we'll refund unused credits.
    </p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep Inlay running and correct, but we can't promise it will always be available or free of errors, and we may change or stop
      features. If we ever stop HD mode, we'll refund unused credits from packs bought in the 12 months before.
    </p>
    <p>
      Inlay, the Inlay name and its logo belong to us. As far as the law allows, Inlay is provided as is, and our total liability to you is
      limited to what you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have as a consumer that can't
      be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms; the date below shows when. Significant changes will be shown on the site before they take effect.</p>

    <p class="fine">Last updated {UPDATED}.</p>
  </article>
</Page>
